Obrii Meshtastic PSK/PKI core and remote administration

Independent C++ implementation of the publicly documented Meshtastic wire
format and protobuf field definitions. No Meshtastic firmware source or
generated protobuf code is included. Protocol references are listed in
docs/meshtastic_core.md. This is not a distribution of Meshtastic firmware.

AES primitive: existing third_party/tiny_aes (tiny-AES-c, kokke), revision
23856752fbd139da0b8ca6e471a13d5bcc99a08d, Unlicense/public domain.
The two wrappers compile the existing source in separate C++ namespaces for
AES-128 and AES-256 CTR without changing the DMR crypto build.
Redistribute third_party/tiny_aes/unlicense.txt with this component.

Optional LoRa adapter: uses ObriiLoRa. Retain its NOTICE and LICENSE.LoRaPHY
as installed by that library. See src/lora/NOTICE for upstream attribution.

PKI cryptographic primitives use the operating-system Windows CNG provider
(bcrypt), or an externally supplied OpenSSL Crypto library on other platforms.
No X25519/SHA256/AES-CCM implementation is vendored here. Binary distributions
that supply OpenSSL must also supply that dependency's applicable notices.
PKI fixture keys are the public RFC7748 test vectors, not operational keys.
